# ArcGPT Frontend — environment
#
# This project is a static browser bundle. It holds NO secrets: no database
# credentials, no LLM keys, no backend session secrets. Everything sensitive
# lives in ../backend/.env and is only ever read by the Express server.

# Base URL of ArcGPT-Backend.
#
# Leave this UNSET for the normal setup. ArcGPT-Backend serves this bundle and
# the API from the same origin, which is required in practice: the session
# cookie it issues is `sameSite: 'strict'`, so a separately-hosted frontend on
# another port would never present it and every API call would 401.
#
# Only set it when the frontend is genuinely deployed somewhere else, e.g.
#   VITE_BACKEND_URL=https://arcgpt-api.example.com
#
# Note: everything prefixed with VITE_ is inlined into the public bundle at
# build time. Never put a credential in this file.
